Signoff-Tradeoff: Centering-only PCA's scale-comparability justification only holds at the post-final-norm layer; intermediate raw-residual-stream layers (1, 14/16) may have PC1 dominated by high-variance outlier features, mitigated but not eliminated by per-layer shuffled-label control and Spearman checks.
Signoff-Tradeoff: Unbalanced num_invalid_fields groups in line/train (min 4573 rows) get no CI or reweighting treatment in the Spearman/centroid analysis; accepted since these are early exploratory measurements not yet feeding into published results.
Signoff-Risk: verify_read_point's determinism check is a single-point spot check per run, not a per-row guarantee; a late-run nondeterministic bf16-GPU row would be silently logged as reproducible.
Signoff-Risk: metrics.json's judge_accuracy excludes rather than penalizes unrecognised-verdict rows, which can mask degraded performance if recognition failures correlate with harder examples; the only hard gate on this (verdict_recognised_rate >= 0.95) lives in analysis/representations.py's load_run, not in run_experiment.py itself.
Signoff-Risk: Walltime budgets for the GPU jobs (e.g. 48h line/train) are unconfirmed estimates on a shared mcnet allocation; mitigated by collect()'s per-document cache-resume, not by a validated timing measurement.
